1
00:00:07,068 --> 00:00:10,037
Mom, Dad, I found cigarettes
in Greg's jacket.

2
00:00:10,138 --> 00:00:12,367
-Greg, were you smoking cigarettes?
-No, Dad.

3
00:00:12,474 --> 00:00:14,374
He's lying. There's no doubt about that.

4
00:00:14,476 --> 00:00:17,842
Greg, I'm afraid your punishment
will be four hours in the snakepit.

5
00:00:17,946 --> 00:00:20,175
That'll give you time to think about
what you did.

6
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,473
Man!

7
00:00:22,183 --> 00:00:23,150
That'll teach him.

8
00:00:23,251 --> 00:00:25,980
Jan, I'm afraid you've earned
a day in the fire chamber...

9
00:00:26,087 --> 00:00:27,747
...for tattling on your brother.

10
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:32,454
Smoking. How does
a boy like that go so wrong?

11
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,721
-They live in a crummy neighborhood.
-The Bradys?

12
00:00:34,829 --> 00:00:38,060
Yeah. They got robbers, thugs,
drug dealers. You name it.

13
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:39,632
You folks want some pancakes?

14
00:00:39,734 --> 00:00:43,170
No, thanks. See, that's the worst
we got is Jemima's Witnesses.

15
00:00:43,904 --> 00:00:46,896
"It seems today that all you see"

16
00:00:47,242 --> 00:00:50,473
"is violence in movies and sex on TV"

17
00:00:50,578 --> 00:00:53,978
"But where are those good,
old-fashioned values"

18
00:00:54,081 --> 00:00:56,641
"on which we used to rely?"

19
00:00:57,418 --> 00:01:00,387
"Lucky there's a family guy"

20
00:01:00,488 --> 00:01:03,615
"Lucky there's a man who'll
positively tell you"

21
00:01:03,724 --> 00:01:05,453
"all the things that make us"

22
00:01:05,559 --> 00:01:07,049
"laugh 'n' cry"

23
00:01:07,162 --> 00:01:11,825
"He's a family guy"

24
00:01:17,505 --> 00:01:20,735
Mom, my lips are too thin.
Can I please get collagen injections?

25
00:01:20,841 --> 00:01:23,309
Meg, you don't need to change
the way you look.

26
00:01:23,411 --> 00:01:26,811
You know, most of the world's problems
stem from poor self-image.

27
00:01:36,323 --> 00:01:39,315
Excellent! The mind-control device
is nearing completion!

28
00:01:39,427 --> 00:01:41,724
Stewie, I said no toys at the table.

29
00:01:41,829 --> 00:01:43,022
Damn you, vile woman!

30
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:46,496
You've impeded my work since the day
I escaped from your wretched womb.

31
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:49,659
Don't pout, honey. When you were born...

32
00:01:49,770 --> 00:01:53,331
...the doctor said you were
the happiest looking baby he'd ever seen.

33
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,536
But, of course. That was my victory day.
The fruition of my deeply-laid plans...

34
00:01:57,644 --> 00:02:01,842
...to escape from that cursed ovarian
bastille! Return the device, woman!

35
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:03,473
No toys, Stewie.

36
00:02:03,585 --> 00:02:04,551
Very well, then.

37
00:02:04,652 --> 00:02:08,587
Mark my words, when you least expect it,
your uppance will come!

38
00:02:10,657 --> 00:02:12,022
Mom, can I turn the heat up?

39
00:02:12,126 --> 00:02:15,185
Don't touch the thermostat, Meg.
Your father gets upset.

40
00:02:15,295 --> 00:02:17,285
Come on. This thing goes up to 90.

41
00:02:17,397 --> 00:02:18,329
Who touched the thermostat?

42
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:19,990
God, how does he always know?

43
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:22,295
Brain implant, Meg. Every father's got one.

44
00:02:22,403 --> 00:02:24,302
Tells you when the kids mess with the dial.

45
00:02:24,404 --> 00:02:26,371
My thing went off!
Your thermostat okay?

46
00:02:26,473 --> 00:02:28,373
-Yeah, it's all right.
-Is my kid over here?

47
00:02:28,476 --> 00:02:29,533
Forget it! False alarm!

48
00:02:30,211 --> 00:02:31,871
Ass ahoy.

49
00:02:31,979 --> 00:02:35,470
Peter, it's 7:00 and you've still got
your pants on. What's the occasion?

50
00:02:35,582 --> 00:02:37,140
He's going to a stag party.

51
00:02:37,252 --> 00:02:39,913
Lois, I work hard all week
to provide for this family.

52
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,247
I am the man of the house.

53
00:02:41,355 --> 00:02:44,552
As the man, I order you
to give me permission to go to this party.

54
00:02:44,658 --> 00:02:48,286
Look, at least promise me you won't drink.
Alcohol always leads to trouble.

55
00:02:48,695 --> 00:02:50,424
Come on. You're worrying about nothing.

56
00:02:50,598 --> 00:02:54,261
Remember when you got drunk
off the Communion wine at church?

57
00:02:54,702 --> 00:02:57,670
And so the Lord God smote poor Job...

58
00:02:57,804 --> 00:03:00,136
...with festering boils all over his body.

59
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:02,401
Man, I hate it when he tells this story.

60
00:03:02,542 --> 00:03:06,705
Yet, miraculously,
Job was still able to retain his dignity.

61
00:03:06,813 --> 00:03:10,146
-Is that really the blood of Christ?
-Yes.

62
00:03:10,384 --> 00:03:13,376
Man, that guy must've been wasted
24 hours a day.

63
00:03:14,054 --> 00:03:16,750
And then there was that time
at the ice cream store.

64
00:03:17,190 --> 00:03:19,487
Butter Rum's my favorite.

65
00:03:21,595 --> 00:03:24,826
Remember you had an lrish coffee
the day we went to see PhiIadeIphia?

66
00:03:30,637 --> 00:03:34,198
I got it. That's the guy from Big.
Tom Hanks, that's it.

67
00:03:34,441 --> 00:03:37,375
Funny guy, Tom Hanks.
Everything he says is a stitch.

68
00:03:37,477 --> 00:03:38,739
I have AIDS.

69
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:42,877
-Promise me, Peter.
-Lois, honey, I promise.

70
00:03:42,983 --> 00:03:45,815
Not a drop of alcohol is gonna touch
these lips tonight.

71
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:47,819
Who wants to play Drink The Beer?

72
00:03:47,921 --> 00:03:49,320
Right here.

73
00:03:49,423 --> 00:03:51,014
-You win.
-All right. What do I win?

74
00:03:51,124 --> 00:03:52,182
Another beer!

75
00:03:52,292 --> 00:03:53,850
I'm going for the high score!

76
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,189
Actually, Charlie's got the high score.

77
00:03:56,296 --> 00:03:58,160
Man. Your clock won't flush.

78
00:03:59,266 --> 00:04:02,257
I feel kind of bad, guys.
I promised my wife I wouldn't drink.

79
00:04:02,369 --> 00:04:05,270
-Don't feel bad, Peter.
-Gee. I never thought of it like that.

80
00:04:05,505 --> 00:04:06,732
Did you bring the porno?

81
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,469
Did I bring the porno?
You're gonna love it. It's a classic.

82
00:04:11,111 --> 00:04:13,010
Listen, Ilsa. If I take this thing out...

83
00:04:13,113 --> 00:04:16,105
...and you're not on it, you'll regret it.
Not today or tomorrow.

84
00:04:16,216 --> 00:04:18,183
But soon, and for the rest of your Iife.

85
00:04:18,285 --> 00:04:19,945
Come on, Ilsa! Get on it!

86
00:04:23,223 --> 00:04:25,417
The statue was a gift from France.

87
00:04:25,525 --> 00:04:26,685
What is this?

88
00:04:26,793 --> 00:04:29,590
Man. My kid must've taped
over this for history class.

89
00:04:30,864 --> 00:04:33,388
The Statue of Liberty?
What are we gonna do?

90
00:04:33,499 --> 00:04:37,832
-Boys, we're gonna drink till she's hot.
-That's just crazy enough to work.

91
00:04:43,543 --> 00:04:45,169
Meg, finish your pancakes.

92
00:04:45,278 --> 00:04:48,007
-Chris, elbows off your father.
-Thanks, son.

93
00:04:48,114 --> 00:04:51,880
37 beers. You're setting
a great example for the kids, Peter.

94
00:04:51,985 --> 00:04:55,113
Yeah. A new family record.
Way to raise the bar, Dad.

95
00:04:55,222 --> 00:04:57,212
Chris, you're 13. Don't talk like that.

96
00:04:57,323 --> 00:04:59,883
Kids, Daddy only drank
so the Statue of Liberty...

97
00:04:59,993 --> 00:05:01,392
...would take her clothes off.

98
00:05:01,495 --> 00:05:04,986
-What did you promise me last night?
-I wouldn't drink at the stag party.

99
00:05:05,098 --> 00:05:07,965
-And what did you do?
-Drank at the stag....

100
00:05:08,067 --> 00:05:11,127
I almost walked right into that one. God!

101
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:14,297
Feels like accountants
are cranking adding machines in my head.

102
00:05:18,778 --> 00:05:21,645
Dick, you ever wonder
what's outside those walls?

103
00:05:21,748 --> 00:05:24,716
That's dangerous thinking, Paul.
You best stick to your work.

104
00:05:24,818 --> 00:05:25,785
Okay.

105
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:30,580
You see? A hangover is nature's way
of telling you I was right. I mean....

106
00:05:30,689 --> 00:05:32,553
Mom, are you all right?

107
00:05:32,658 --> 00:05:36,355
My goodness.
This chair leg was loose. Isn't that silly?

108
00:05:36,463 --> 00:05:38,453
I could've broken my neck.

109
00:05:38,632 --> 00:05:39,689
Damn!

110
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,734
Honey. I took a cab home,
I slept on the table...

111
00:05:43,837 --> 00:05:46,134
...so I wouldn't wake you up.
Nothing bad happened.

112
00:05:46,239 --> 00:05:48,070
I guess you're right.

113
00:05:48,175 --> 00:05:50,836
Apology accepted.
All right, I'm going to work.

114
00:05:50,943 --> 00:05:52,705
Somebody's gotta put food on this table.

115
00:05:56,382 --> 00:05:57,713
How are you coming, Johnson?

116
00:05:57,818 --> 00:06:00,149
Mr. Weed, I've been working
on the new G.I. Jew line.

117
00:06:00,252 --> 00:06:02,413
And as you can see, they look great.

118
00:06:02,521 --> 00:06:03,545
You call these bagels?

119
00:06:03,657 --> 00:06:05,954
I'm glad he's on our side!

120
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,451
Peter!
What?

121
00:06:09,562 --> 00:06:10,755
Are you sleeping on the job?

122
00:06:10,863 --> 00:06:14,025
No. There's a bug in my eye
and I'm trying to suffocate him.

123
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:17,967
Peter, I like you. But l need you to be
more than just eye candy around here.

124
00:06:18,071 --> 00:06:21,198
It's your job to watch for toys
that could be hazardous to kids.

125
00:06:21,307 --> 00:06:23,537
-Now, look sharp!
-Yes, sir!

126
00:06:35,387 --> 00:06:40,050
And now back to Action News 5.
Our top story tonight, "When Toys Attack."

127
00:06:40,159 --> 00:06:41,785
Quite a situation we've got here, Tom.

128
00:06:41,894 --> 00:06:44,260
Quite a situation we've got here, Tom,
indeed, Diane.

129
00:06:44,363 --> 00:06:47,264
The Happy-Go-Lucky Toy Company
of Quahog, Rhode lsland...

130
00:06:47,366 --> 00:06:50,425
...has released highly unsafe
products into the retail market.

131
00:06:50,804 --> 00:06:52,896
Come on, Timmy! Throw the Silly Ball!

132
00:06:54,773 --> 00:06:56,798
Boy! A Pound Poochie!

133
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:00,500
Come on, Baby Heimlich, spit it out.

134
00:07:03,182 --> 00:07:04,273
Peter, I'm appalled.

135
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:07,215
Your negligence has damaged
this company's reputation.

136
00:07:07,319 --> 00:07:08,307
You're fired!

137
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:09,613
Jeez. For how long?

138
00:07:12,191 --> 00:07:13,681
My God! You got fired?

139
00:07:13,792 --> 00:07:17,420
-Way to go, Dad! Fight the machine!
-How do you know about the machine?

140
00:07:17,530 --> 00:07:20,260
Don't worry.
I'll still put food on this table.

141
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:22,926
Just not as much.
So it might get a little competitive.

142
00:07:23,035 --> 00:07:27,563
Who cares about food? Now we'll never
be able to afford my lip injections!

143
00:07:27,706 --> 00:07:30,072
Can we put her
out in the yard for a while?

144
00:07:30,175 --> 00:07:32,165
Okay, who's hungry?

145
00:07:32,645 --> 00:07:34,976
Jeez. How the hell
am l gonna break this to Lois?

146
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:38,607
If she finds out I got fired for drinking,
she's gonna blame me!

147
00:07:38,717 --> 00:07:42,175
Lie to her. It's okay to lie
to women. They're not people like us.

148
00:07:42,288 --> 00:07:44,778
I don't know. Hey, where's the other guy?

149
00:07:46,025 --> 00:07:48,653
Come on, you bastard! I'm late for work.

150
00:07:48,761 --> 00:07:49,886
This is perfect!

151
00:07:50,462 --> 00:07:52,692
Look, I don't want your mom to worry,
all right?

152
00:07:52,798 --> 00:07:55,197
When she worries, she says,
"I told you so" and:

153
00:07:55,301 --> 00:07:59,202
"Stop doing that. I'm asleep."
So l'm just gonna tell a little lie, okay?

154
00:07:59,305 --> 00:08:01,636
Not a word to your mom
about me getting canned.

155
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:03,139
What's that, Peter?

156
00:08:03,242 --> 00:08:06,234
-Nothing. The lost-my-job smells great.
-What?

157
00:08:06,345 --> 00:08:09,336
Meg, honey, can you pass
the fired-my-ass-for-negligence?

158
00:08:09,448 --> 00:08:11,108
Peter, are you feeling okay?

159
00:08:11,216 --> 00:08:13,877
I feel great!
I haven't got a job in the world.

160
00:08:13,985 --> 00:08:15,611
All right, then let's eat.

161
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,416
I know you all hate eggplant, but....

162
00:08:19,558 --> 00:08:21,422
What on earth was that?

163
00:08:23,896 --> 00:08:26,592
What the deuce are you staring at?
It's tuna fish...

164
00:08:26,998 --> 00:08:28,090
...and nothing else.

165
00:08:32,538 --> 00:08:33,970
How's your job search going?

166
00:08:34,073 --> 00:08:37,337
It sucks, Brian. I've already
been through two jobs this week.

167
00:08:37,443 --> 00:08:38,966
I got fired off of that commercial.

168
00:08:39,078 --> 00:08:41,740
Try it again.
"I'm caca for Cocoa Puffs."

169
00:08:41,847 --> 00:08:43,575
No, damn it! Take 26!

170
00:08:44,049 --> 00:08:47,449
Then I had that job as the sneeze guard
for that restaurant's salad bar.

171
00:08:50,122 --> 00:08:51,282
Take it outside, lady.

172
00:08:51,624 --> 00:08:53,716
I thought I could win money
in that talent show.

173
00:08:54,093 --> 00:08:57,528
And the prize goes
to The von Trapp Family Singers!

174
00:08:57,830 --> 00:08:58,921
That is bull....

175
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,264
Peter, I know it's a dangerous precedent...

176
00:09:03,368 --> 00:09:05,598
...but you might want to tell Lois the truth.

177
00:09:05,704 --> 00:09:08,832
What? That I can't provide for my family?
That she's always right?

178
00:09:08,941 --> 00:09:11,374
That I didn't stand up to a tank
in Tiananmen Square?

179
00:09:15,947 --> 00:09:18,848
Screw this!
I just came over to buy some fireworks!

180
00:09:19,385 --> 00:09:21,682
You can't keep lying to her
about losing your job.

181
00:09:21,786 --> 00:09:24,413
Eventually, she'll find out
where you're going every day.

182
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:25,454
Yeah.

183
00:09:28,694 --> 00:09:31,254
Yeah, you're right.
Okay, I'll tell her tonight.

184
00:09:48,047 --> 00:09:49,536
Victory is mine!

185
00:09:49,947 --> 00:09:51,881
I'll need the checkbook
in the morning.

186
00:09:51,984 --> 00:09:54,009
I'm going to Stop 'N Shop
for some sweet corn.

187
00:09:54,119 --> 00:09:55,779
You're spending money on food again?

188
00:09:55,888 --> 00:09:57,514
Lois, we just had dinner.

189
00:09:57,623 --> 00:10:01,752
I enjoyed it so much,
I thought we'd eat again tomorrow.

190
00:10:01,859 --> 00:10:04,453
Since when are you so concerned
about our food budget?

191
00:10:04,562 --> 00:10:05,755
I just....

192
00:10:05,863 --> 00:10:09,025
Lois, this is really hard for me to say, but....

193
00:10:09,133 --> 00:10:10,930
What is it, Peter?

194
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:14,197
-You're getting kind of fat.
-What?

195
00:10:14,305 --> 00:10:16,569
It's just.... It's not healthy.

196
00:10:16,675 --> 00:10:19,973
Peter, I do my Jane Fonda workout tape
three times a week.

197
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:21,942
When was the last time you saw your toes?

198
00:10:22,046 --> 00:10:24,536
I thought you people were
supposed to be jolly.

199
00:10:24,649 --> 00:10:26,947
Peter, what the hell is the matter with you?

200
00:10:27,051 --> 00:10:30,145
Honey, if there's something wrong,
you can tell me.

201
00:10:30,288 --> 00:10:34,156
-Sorry, man. Am I late? What did I miss?
-Thank God you're here. What do I do?

202
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:36,488
Tell him to keep quiet. He's in too deep.

203
00:10:36,595 --> 00:10:38,186
I don't know.

204
00:10:38,529 --> 00:10:39,655
Where's the other guy?

205
00:10:40,965 --> 00:10:42,488
This is unbelievable!

206
00:10:43,535 --> 00:10:46,799
I promise you, everything's fine.
You got nothing to worry about.

207
00:10:46,904 --> 00:10:50,066
Well, well, Mother!
We meet again!

208
00:10:50,174 --> 00:10:52,698
Stewie, l thought
I tucked you in an hour ago.

209
00:10:52,810 --> 00:10:55,938
Not tightly enough it would seem.
And now you contemptible harpy...

210
00:10:56,047 --> 00:10:58,515
...I shall end your reign
of matriarchal tyranny.

211
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,550
You can play tomorrow, honey.

212
00:11:00,652 --> 00:11:02,141
Right now it's bedtime.

213
00:11:02,821 --> 00:11:05,220
Blast you and your estrogenical treachery!

214
00:11:05,323 --> 00:11:06,620
Sweet dreams, kiddo.

215
00:11:06,724 --> 00:11:08,088
You have the power to end this!

216
00:11:11,195 --> 00:11:12,559
How'd she take it?

217
00:11:12,663 --> 00:11:14,528
I told her she was fat.

218
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:15,893
No.

219
00:11:16,601 --> 00:11:18,397
I hate lying to Lois. lt's just....

220
00:11:18,503 --> 00:11:20,596
It's the best way
to keep her from the truth.

221
00:11:20,705 --> 00:11:23,172
You have no choice.
Your unemployment will dry up soon.

222
00:11:23,274 --> 00:11:26,710
She'll probably sense something's amiss
when they repossess your house.

223
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:29,041
You really oughta think
of your family's welfare.

224
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:30,613
Jeez, Brian! That's a great idea!

225
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:37,015
Okay, do you have any disabilities,
past injuries, physical anomalies?

226
00:11:37,789 --> 00:11:40,417
I didn't have gas
for the first time until I was 30.

227
00:11:44,929 --> 00:11:46,793
What the hell was that?

228
00:11:48,366 --> 00:11:51,699
Guys, our money problems
are over! We're officially on welfare.

229
00:11:51,803 --> 00:11:54,236
Come on, help me scatter car parts
on the front lawn.

230
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:55,498
How much are we getting?

231
00:11:55,606 --> 00:11:57,870
Let's see. $150 a week.

232
00:11:58,376 --> 00:12:00,105
Wait. That's a comma, not a decimal.

233
00:12:02,246 --> 00:12:03,234
Whoops.

234
00:12:03,614 --> 00:12:05,878
No, I haven't seen Peter all afternoon.

235
00:12:05,983 --> 00:12:07,574
I was giving a piano lesson.

236
00:12:08,419 --> 00:12:10,649
Stewie, why don't you play
in the other room?

237
00:12:10,755 --> 00:12:12,085
